- internal: the Chinese mainland.
- overseas: outside the Chinese mainland.

Do not specify this parameter for the IP_RANGE mode.', example='internal'),
  matchType?: string(name='MatchType', description='The match type. Valid values:
- LINE: the line mode.
- IP_RANGE: the client IP address range mode.

If this parameter is omitted, it is processed as LINE. To create an IP address range policy, you must explicitly set this parameter to IP_RANGE and provide ClientIpRanges. You cannot provide LineId or Paths at the same time. The match type cannot be changed after creation.', example='IP_RANGE'),
  pathsShrink?: string(name='Paths', description='The line selection path that describes the line conditions at each level. This parameter applies only to the LINE mode. The IP_RANGE mode does not use line paths. When you create a line policy, provide valid options at each level. Use x for the default option. For the Chinese mainland, the levels include ISP, region, and province. For regions outside the Chinese mainland, the levels include continent and region.'),
